---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Had It Gone"
  description="How Had It Gone handles data, local storage, and privacy. We do not collect personal data and we do not use tracking cookies."
  url="https://haditgone.com/privacy"
  type="website"
>
  <div class="about-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p>
      <em>Last updated: October 2026</em>
    </p>

    <h2>What This Policy Covers</h2>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Had It Gone</strong> handles data when you visit <strong>haditgone.com</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>The Short Version</h2>

    <p>
      We do not collect personal data. We do not use tracking cookies. We do not use third-party analytics. We do not sell or share data about our visitors. Any data we store is stored locally in your browser and never reaches us.
    </p>

    <h2>What We Do Not Collect</h2>

    <p>When you browse Had It Gone, we do not:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>collect your name, email address, or any other personal information;</li>
      <li>set cookies on your device for tracking or advertising purposes;</li>
      <li>use analytics tools that identify individual visitors;</li>
      <li>share or sell any information about our visitors to third parties.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What Happens When You Visit</h2>

    <p>
      Like any website, Had It Gone is served through a hosting provider. Our site is hosted on <strong>Netlify</strong>, which processes standard technical information required to deliver the website to your browser.
    </p>

    <p>
      This includes your IP address, the pages you request, your browser type, and basic request metadata. This information is processed by Netlify for the purpose of serving the site and protecting it from abuse. It is not used by Had It Gone to identify individual visitors.
    </p>

    <p>
      Netlify operates under its own privacy policy and is responsible for how it handles this technical data.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>

    <p>
      Had It Gone does not set any cookies of its own — neither for tracking, nor for advertising, nor for analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>Local Storage</h2>

    <p>
      Had It Gone uses your browser's local storage to remember a small number of settings and preferences. This data is stored only on your device, is not transmitted to us, and is not accessible to us. It includes:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Theme preference</strong> — whether you have chosen light or dark mode;</li>
      <li><strong>Bookmarks</strong> — articles you have chosen to save for later;</li>
      <li><strong>Reading progress</strong> — how far you have scrolled in articles you have started, used to show you a "Continue Reading" section on the homepage.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      This information never leaves your browser. We have no way to access it. You can clear it at any time through your browser settings, and it will also disappear if you clear your browsing data.
    </p>

    <h2>No Analytics</h2>

    <p>
      We do not use Google Analytics, Plausible, or any other analytics service. We do not measure traffic, track reading behaviour on the server side, or build profiles of our visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>External Links</h2>

    <p>
      Articles may contain links to external websites. If you follow one of those links, the privacy policy of that website applies — not ours. We are not responsible for how other websites handle your data.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing Buttons</h2>

    <p>
      Articles include buttons for sharing on external platforms such as X, Facebook, LinkedIn, and Reddit. These buttons are simple links — they do not load external scripts or set cookies until you click them. Once you click, the platform you chose handles the interaction under its own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>RSS Feed</h2>

    <p>
      Had It Gone offers an RSS feed at <strong>/rss.xml</strong>. Reading the feed does not involve any data collection by us. Your RSS reader may have its own privacy practices, which we do not control.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>

    <p>
      Had It Gone is a general-interest history and science website. It is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect any personal data from anyone.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Rights</h2>

    <p>
      Because we do not collect personal data, there is nothing for us to access, correct, or delete on your behalf. The data stored in your browser is under your control — you can view it, modify it, or remove it at any time through your browser settings. If you have questions about this policy, you can contact us using the email below.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>

    <p>
      If we ever change how Had It Gone handles data — for example, if we add analytics or a newsletter — we will update this page and change the date at the top. We encourage you to check back if you want to stay informed.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>

    <p>
      📧 <a href="mailto:hello@haditgone.com">hello@haditgone.com</a>
    </p>

    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Homepage</a>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>